WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:16.888
A few days later, Cedric was leaving the castle to visit his mother.

2
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.172
He expected to ride in the earl's carriage, pulled by two horses.

3
00:00:23.594 --> 00:00:27.437
Instead a small carriage with one horse and a driver waited for him.

4
00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:34.197
"That's a present for your mother," said the earl, who had followed Cedric outside.

5
00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:39.199
"She shouldn't walk to church or anywhere else she wants to go."

6
00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:42.541
"Oh, Grandpapa!"

7
00:00:43.861 --> 00:00:46.182
Cedric could hardly contain his excitement.

8
00:00:46.202 --> 00:00:49.424
"You're the kindest man in the world!

9
00:00:50.444 --> 00:00:53.546
Wait until Mama sees her own horse and carriage!"

10
00:00:55.146 --> 00:00:58.508
Then Cedric noticed that the earl wasn't dressed to go visiting.

11
00:01:00.056 --> 00:01:01.597
"Where's your hat, Grandpapa?

12
00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:03.538
Where are your gloves?

13
00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:05.959
You're coming with me, right?

14
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.541
I'm sure Mama will want to thank you in person."

15
00:01:11.162 --> 00:01:12.343
The earl shook his head.

16
00:01:12.363 --> 00:01:16.225
"Tell your mother this is a present from you.

17
00:01:18.466 --> 00:01:19.587
Now hurry back here."

18
00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:25.390
Cedric climbed into the carriage and called out the window.

19
00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.712
"Are you sure you won't come along?"

20
00:01:31.712 --> 00:01:35.896
"Yes, and remember that this is a present from you, not me."

21
00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.840
Cedric was always eager to see his mother.

22
00:01:41.921 --> 00:01:45.403
But that day the short ride to her house seemed longer than usual.

23
00:01:49.507 --> 00:01:53.290
wish the driver could make the horse go faster," Cedric thought.

24
00:01:55.292 --> 00:02:00.196
When they finally arrived at the cottage, Cedric's mother was cutting flowers in the front garden.

25
00:02:03.176 --> 00:02:05.457
"Mama! Look what I brought you!"

26
00:02:05.977 --> 00:02:07.497
Cedric called from the carriage.

27
00:02:09.138 --> 00:02:12.359
Cedric's mother approached the carriage with a bouquet in her arms.

28
00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:15.420
"It's your own carriage!"

29
00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.180
Cedric said proudly.

30
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.922
"Whenever you want to go somewhere, this man will drive you."

31
00:02:23.362 --> 00:02:26.603
Mrs. Errol looked up at the man holding the horse's reins.

32
00:02:27.703 --> 00:02:28.964
He tipped his hat to her.

33
00:02:30.836 --> 00:02:34.197
"Grandpapa said I must tell you that it's a present from me!"

34
00:02:34.678 --> 00:02:35.398
Cedric said.

35
00:02:35.418 --> 00:02:38.279
"Even though I know it's really from him.

36
00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.580
Isn't he the kindest man in the world?"

37
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:45.622
"It's a beautiful carriage."

38
00:02:47.003 --> 00:02:49.204
Mrs. Errol reached out to pat the horse.

39
00:02:50.944 --> 00:02:53.325
She didn't want to accept this gift from the earl.

40
00:02:54.286 --> 00:02:57.067
But she also didn't want to spoil her son's happiness.

41
00:02:57.087 --> 00:02:59.788
"Let's go for a ride."

42
00:03:01.096 --> 00:03:03.837
Cedric hopped from the carriage and held open the door.

43
00:03:03.857 --> 00:03:07.679
"I must put these flowers in the house first."

44
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.761
Cedric insisted, however, that they go right that minute.

45
00:03:14.262 --> 00:03:14.722
So Mrs.

46
00:03:14.862 --> 00:03:17.003
Errol let herself be taken for a drive.

47
00:03:18.204 --> 00:03:21.185
The whole time Cedric happily talked about his grandfather.

48
00:03:23.926 --> 00:03:28.088
By the time they returned home, his mother had a better attitude toward the earl.

49
00:03:29.364 --> 00:03:31.746
"I'm glad you see the goodness in your grandfather."

50
00:03:32.787 --> 00:03:35.108
Mrs. Errol put her arm around her son.

51
00:03:35.128 --> 00:03:37.890
"He has so few friends."

52
00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:40.792
"You're wrong, Mama!

53
00:03:41.393 --> 00:03:43.154
Everyone likes Grandpapa."

54
00:03:45.996 --> 00:03:48.418
That night Cedric wrote a letter to his friend Mr.

55
00:03:48.458 --> 00:03:49.478
Hobbs, the grocer.

56
00:03:50.559 --> 00:03:53.621
Cedric described his rooms and the castle and the park.

57
00:03:55.363 --> 00:03:56.944
He talked about learning to ride.

58
00:03:57.956 --> 00:04:00.098
But he mostly wrote about his grandfather.

59
00:04:01.578 --> 00:04:06.041
You said all earls were tyrants, but my grandfather isn't one.

60
00:04:07.022 --> 00:04:09.223
In fact, I think you'd like him.

61
00:04:10.684 --> 00:04:13.806
So far I haven't seen his velvet robe and coronet.

62
00:04:15.426 --> 00:04:16.947
Then he wrote about his mother.

63
00:04:18.668 --> 00:04:21.950
Most of the time I'm happy living with my grandfather.

64
00:04:22.851 --> 00:04:24.532
Except when I miss my mother.

65
00:04:25.576 --> 00:04:27.638
I wish she could live at the castle with me.

66
00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:33.343
After Cedric finished his letter, he showed it to the earl.

67
00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:35.825
"Would you check the spelling for me?"

68
00:04:37.466 --> 00:04:40.108
The earl slowly read both sides of the paper.

69
00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:47.254
When he finished, he asked, "Do you miss your mother very much?"

70
00:04:47.274 --> 00:04:50.677
"I miss her all the time."

71
00:04:52.118 --> 00:04:54.280
Cedric laid a hand on the earl's arm.

72
00:04:55.468 --> 00:04:58.409
"But you don't miss her, do you?"

73
00:04:58.429 --> 00:05:03.650
"I don't know her at all," the earl said.

74
00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:10.072
"I've always wondered about that, but Mama told me not to ask you any questions."

75
00:05:11.493 --> 00:05:14.254
Cedric paused, hoping the earl would say more.

76
00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:20.676
When the old man stayed silent, Cedric said, "I won't ask you again.

77
00:05:26.988 --> 00:05:28.209
Good-night." For a while Mr.

78
00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:30.950
Hobbs pretended that Cedric hadn't really gone away.

79
00:05:32.351 --> 00:05:35.313
He was sure that one day his young friend would reappear.

80
00:05:36.814 --> 00:05:39.075
But, of course, that didn't happen.

81
00:05:40.876 --> 00:05:43.758
Cedric's letter made the grocer miss his friend even more.

82
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:47.380
Mr. Hobbs read and reread the letter.

83
00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:50.641
He folded it up and sighed.

84
00:05:50.661 --> 00:05:54.884
"I'll never forget you, Cedric."

85
00:05:57.396 --> 00:05:58.257
That night Mr.

86
00:05:58.297 --> 00:06:01.720
Hobbs slowly walked down the street to the house where Cedric had lived.

87
00:06:03.121 --> 00:06:05.783
There was still a For Rent sign in the front window.

88
00:06:07.345 --> 00:06:10.407
Mr. Hobbs stared at the house before returning to the store.

89
00:06:14.231 --> 00:06:16.553
wish I had someone to talk to."

90
00:06:18.434 --> 00:06:20.976
Mr. Hobbs took Cedric's letter from his pocket.

91
00:06:20.996 --> 00:06:24.820
"It would be nice to share this with someone.

92
00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.496
But I don't know who that would be."
